WEBVTT

00:00:39.581 --> 00:00:41.792
Notify his survivors.

00:00:44.586 --> 00:00:46.171
B-E-N-D-E-R

00:00:46.255 --> 00:00:48.257
Bender!

00:00:48.340 --> 00:00:49.800
B-E-N-D-E-R

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.468
Bender!

00:00:51.552 --> 00:00:53.136
Saying B...

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:55.305
E-N...

00:00:55.389 --> 00:00:57.558
Der!

00:01:00.143 --> 00:01:01.353
Mail call!

00:01:01.436 --> 00:01:04.481
Amy, here's your
designer lingerie catalog.

00:01:04.565 --> 00:01:07.234
Fry, Sadie's Bra Parade.

00:01:07.317 --> 00:01:09.444
And, Leela, Bulk Underpants Outlet.

00:01:09.528 --> 00:01:10.988
You buy one pound of underwear

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:12.698
and you're on their list forever.

00:01:12.781 --> 00:01:16.743
And for Bender, uh-oh,
a black-bordered envelope.

00:01:16.827 --> 00:01:19.288
Oh, no. Someone you know must've died.

00:01:19.872 --> 00:01:21.915
I hope it was one of my enemies.

00:01:21.999 --> 00:01:24.126
Those guys suck.

00:01:24.251 --> 00:01:27.921
Oh, no! My Uncle Vladimir.

00:01:28.005 --> 00:01:29.423
Oh, I'm sorry, Bender.

00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:30.591
When's the funeral?

00:01:30.674 --> 00:01:32.759
Tomorrow, at the family castle.

00:01:32.843 --> 00:01:34.887
Followed by the reading of his will.

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:36.763
Well, I'm rich.

00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:39.433
Goodbye, losers, whom I've always hated.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:42.102
Come on. It'll be fun.

00:01:55.532 --> 00:01:58.493
Uh, pardon me, my good simpleton.

00:01:58.577 --> 00:02:01.205
Could you take us to yon castle?

00:02:02.331 --> 00:02:03.832
Castle?

00:02:05.417 --> 00:02:08.712
Some say unholy things happen up there.

00:02:08.795 --> 00:02:11.381
For example, all of us say that.

00:02:11.507 --> 00:02:14.801
Pfft! Superstitious robot mumbo jumbo.

00:02:14.885 --> 00:02:18.847
Mumbo, perhaps. Jumbo, perhaps not.

00:02:18.931 --> 00:02:20.641
With all your modern science

00:02:20.724 --> 00:02:22.476
are you any closer to understanding

00:02:22.559 --> 00:02:25.771
the mystery of how a robot walks or talks?

00:02:25.854 --> 00:02:27.272
Yes, you idiot.

00:02:27.356 --> 00:02:28.649
The circuit diagram is

00:02:28.732 --> 00:02:31.318
right here on the inside
of your case.

00:02:31.401 --> 00:02:35.614
I choose to believe
what I was programmed to believe.

00:02:42.287 --> 00:02:44.790
I will go this far and no further.

00:02:47.918 --> 00:02:51.922
And so we commend
Vladimir's remains to the earth.

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:56.218
Filings to filings, rust to rust.

00:03:14.319 --> 00:03:18.031
To my loyal butler "you there,"
for his decades of service,

00:03:18.115 --> 00:03:19.533
I leave a pittance

00:03:19.616 --> 00:03:22.327
to be paid in 20 equal installments

00:03:22.411 --> 00:03:24.746
of 1/20th of a pittance each.

00:03:26.373 --> 00:03:29.251
To my lazy, spoiled son Tandy,

00:03:29.334 --> 00:03:31.795
who never learned the value of a dollar,

00:03:31.962 --> 00:03:34.923
I leave my entire $10 million fortune.

00:03:35.007 --> 00:03:36.216
Is that a lot?

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.635
And to my loving nephew Bender,

00:03:38.719 --> 00:03:41.096
assuming he's not responsible
for my death,

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:42.973
I leave my castle.

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:44.975
Yes! Let's stay there tonight.

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:47.978
On condition that he spend
one night within its walls.

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:51.190
Oh, man, there's always a catch!

00:03:56.111 --> 00:04:01.074
I get a good vibe from this place.

00:04:01.158 --> 00:04:02.743
Nice, long, dinner table.

00:04:02.826 --> 00:04:04.870
Quiet, well-behaved spiders.

00:04:04.953 --> 00:04:06.622
Graveyard adjacent.

00:04:06.705 --> 00:04:08.707
Yep, it's going to be...

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:09.875
What is it?

00:04:09.958 --> 00:04:12.503
That painting. The eyes are watching me.

00:04:12.586 --> 00:04:13.879
Hmm.

00:04:14.713 --> 00:04:18.258
It has motor eye sensors
attached to motion detectors.

00:04:18.342 --> 00:04:19.760
So does my butt,

00:04:19.843 --> 00:04:22.137
but I don't frame it
and put it on the wall.

00:04:22.221 --> 00:04:23.472
Although...

00:04:27.351 --> 00:04:28.435
What's that?

00:04:28.519 --> 00:04:30.437
I don't know, but it's infectious.

00:04:37.528 --> 00:04:40.072
No doubt about it, this place is haunted.

00:04:40.155 --> 00:04:41.490
Don't be silly, mon.

00:04:41.573 --> 00:04:44.409
The last ghost died over 200 years ago.

00:04:44.493 --> 00:04:48.622
The last human ghost, but robot ghosts...

00:04:57.047 --> 00:04:58.257
What does it mean?

00:04:58.340 --> 00:05:00.175
It's just gibberish.

00:05:11.061 --> 00:05:12.855
Uncle Vladimir!

00:05:12.938 --> 00:05:14.314
Come, Bender.

00:05:14.398 --> 00:05:16.775
You'll like being dead.

00:05:16.859 --> 00:05:19.069
That's what they said about being alive.

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:22.698
- Join us.
- Join us.

00:05:22.781 --> 00:05:24.908
Join us, Bender.

00:05:24.992 --> 00:05:27.536
Oh, my God!

00:05:39.089 --> 00:05:40.674
Just as I suspected.

00:05:40.757 --> 00:05:44.511
These robots were buried
in improperly shielded coffins.

00:05:44.595 --> 00:05:47.055
Their programming leaked
into the castle's wiring

00:05:47.139 --> 00:05:48.974
through this old abandoned modem

00:05:49.057 --> 00:05:52.227
allowing them to project
themselves as holograms.

00:05:52.311 --> 00:05:54.646
Of course! It was so obvious.

00:05:54.730 --> 00:05:57.983
Yes, that sequence of words
I said made perfect sense.

00:05:58.066 --> 00:06:01.361
We really should tell Bender
there's nothing to be afraid of.

00:06:08.619 --> 00:06:10.662
Huh?

00:06:18.962 --> 00:06:21.465
No!

00:06:25.302 --> 00:06:30.599
Honk! Honk!

00:06:34.603 --> 00:06:36.605
Bender, wake up.

00:06:38.357 --> 00:06:40.984
He's okay.
Quick, does anyone have any liquor?

00:06:42.945 --> 00:06:44.738
Bender, what happened?

00:06:44.821 --> 00:06:47.115
Somebody tried to run me over.

00:06:47.199 --> 00:06:48.992
And not with a normal hover car.

00:06:49.076 --> 00:06:51.912
It crept along the ground
on round rubber feet.

00:06:51.995 --> 00:06:53.080
Like a wolf.

00:06:53.163 --> 00:06:55.415
Poor Bender, you're seeing things.

00:06:55.499 --> 00:06:57.292
You're drinking too much, or too little.

00:06:57.376 --> 00:06:59.044
I forget how it works with you.

00:06:59.127 --> 00:07:01.672
Anyway, you haven't drunk
exactly the right amount.

00:07:01.755 --> 00:07:03.173
Maybe he has.

00:07:03.257 --> 00:07:05.592
Look at these tracks.

00:07:05.676 --> 00:07:07.928
I think Bender may be telling the truth.

00:07:20.482 --> 00:07:22.109
Bender, you look awful.

00:07:22.192 --> 00:07:24.069
I prescribe makeup.

00:07:24.152 --> 00:07:28.198
Here. It just so happens
I have my Mary Kay sample case.

00:07:28.282 --> 00:07:29.825
I just need sleep.

00:07:29.908 --> 00:07:33.704
I had nightmares all night
about cars running people over.

00:07:33.787 --> 00:07:36.415
Many people dream of a fresh new look.

00:07:36.498 --> 00:07:39.501
And Mary Kay can make
those dreams come true.

00:07:39.585 --> 00:07:42.713
Look at this!
They found those same rubbery tracks

00:07:42.796 --> 00:07:44.423
right here in New New York.

00:07:44.506 --> 00:07:46.925
There was a hit-and-run
by the robot porno theater.

00:07:47.009 --> 00:07:48.844
Robot porno theater?

00:07:48.927 --> 00:07:52.055
I was in that general area last night.

00:07:52.264 --> 00:07:54.141
Whoever ran me down out on the moors

00:07:54.224 --> 00:07:56.310
must've followed me back here.

00:07:56.393 --> 00:07:59.062
Bender, mon,
no one's trying to run you over.

00:07:59.146 --> 00:08:01.190
Stop being a big hallucinating baby.

00:08:01.273 --> 00:08:04.693
Yeah? Well, could a big
hallucinating baby do this?

00:08:08.030 --> 00:08:09.740
I'm scared.

00:08:28.717 --> 00:08:33.680
I don't know which I like more,
smashing cars or smashing faces.

00:08:33.764 --> 00:08:36.225
Well, lucky you don't
got to decide tonight.

00:08:36.308 --> 00:08:38.143
Now, come on, we got church tomorrow.

00:08:48.362 --> 00:08:50.072
Did you hear something?

00:08:50.155 --> 00:08:53.617
Nah, it was probably
just a golden marmoset.

00:08:56.495 --> 00:08:59.915
That don't sound like
no golden marmoset I ever heard.

00:09:06.505 --> 00:09:08.090
- Phew!
- Made it.

00:09:08.173 --> 00:09:10.551
So, anyway,
what are you wearing tomorrow?

00:09:12.886 --> 00:09:15.264
Honk! Honk, honk!

00:09:24.022 --> 00:09:26.859
What the...

00:09:27.985 --> 00:09:29.570
Transmission fluid?

00:09:29.653 --> 00:09:30.779
Where have I been?

00:09:30.863 --> 00:09:31.864
What happened?

00:09:32.114 --> 00:09:34.908
Gets out of here, youse lousy bum.

00:09:35.158 --> 00:09:37.244
Please, I'm scared.

00:09:37.327 --> 00:09:39.580
We're all scared.
It's the human condition.

00:09:39.663 --> 00:09:42.249
Why do you thinks I put
on this tough-guy façade?

00:09:42.332 --> 00:09:43.542
Now, beat it!

00:09:44.501 --> 00:09:46.253
I passed out around midnight,

00:09:46.336 --> 00:09:48.130
which is much earlier than usual.

00:09:48.213 --> 00:09:51.925
And when I woke up,
I found these in my chest cabinet.

00:09:52.050 --> 00:09:53.343
Oh, relax, buddy.

00:09:53.427 --> 00:09:55.679
You were probably just shooting
some big, fuzzy craps.

00:09:55.762 --> 00:09:58.265
No! I think I may have hurt someone.

00:09:58.348 --> 00:10:01.518
Oh, Lord, I'm on the verge
of a nervous meltdown.

00:10:03.395 --> 00:10:06.356
Geez, Bender, you're scaring me.
You're going wacko.

00:10:06.440 --> 00:10:08.650
You're right. I need professional help.

00:10:08.734 --> 00:10:10.402
And damn the expense.

00:10:11.945 --> 00:10:13.697
Damn the expense!

00:10:15.532 --> 00:10:18.327
My friend, you have nothing to worry about

00:10:18.410 --> 00:10:21.705
except a nightmarish life
of unremitting horror.

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:25.876
- Phew!
- For, you see, you are a were-car.

00:10:26.001 --> 00:10:28.086
A were-car?

00:10:28.170 --> 00:10:31.298
The car that ran you down on the moors
was also a were-car.

00:10:31.381 --> 00:10:34.760
It beamed the virus to you
through its demonic headlights.

00:10:34.843 --> 00:10:35.928
That's crazy.

00:10:36.011 --> 00:10:39.306
Yes. So crazy that it must be true.

00:10:39.389 --> 00:10:42.351
Each midnight,
when your clock resets to zero,

00:10:42.434 --> 00:10:46.313
your hardware reconfigures into
a murderous four-wheeled car.

00:10:46.396 --> 00:10:48.565
I can't keep running people over.

00:10:48.649 --> 00:10:50.984
I'm not famous enough to get away with it.

00:10:51.068 --> 00:10:52.361
Can't you help me?

00:10:52.444 --> 00:10:56.198
Yes, but you must be willing
to pay a terrible price.

00:10:56.281 --> 00:10:57.658
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:10:58.534 --> 00:10:59.785
Follow me.

00:11:02.746 --> 00:11:04.540
According to this ancient "read me" file,

00:11:04.623 --> 00:11:08.502
your only hope is
to destroy the original were-car.

00:11:08.585 --> 00:11:11.171
- I'm with you.
- In its death throes,

00:11:11.255 --> 00:11:15.092
the dread car will beam out
the virus's uninstall program.

00:11:15.175 --> 00:11:17.261
Thus, ridding you of the curse.

00:11:17.344 --> 00:11:19.555
And, otherwise, I can never die?

00:11:19.638 --> 00:11:22.516
Who said that? Sure you can die.
You want to die?

00:11:22.599 --> 00:11:23.725
No! I want to live.

00:11:23.809 --> 00:11:25.936
There's still too many things I don't own.

00:11:26.019 --> 00:11:28.397
Then live on, forever cursed.

00:11:28.480 --> 00:11:31.900
Each night, your attacks
will become more gruesome.

00:11:31.984 --> 00:11:33.902
Until one dark night,

00:11:33.986 --> 00:11:37.155
you are doomed to kill
your dearest friend.

00:11:37.281 --> 00:11:40.242
I wouldn't want to be me right now.

00:11:40.325 --> 00:11:43.495
Now, go! Go!

00:11:43.579 --> 00:11:45.998
Uh, could one of you just...

00:11:46.081 --> 00:11:50.544
Forget it. I'll just sleep here.

00:11:57.301 --> 00:11:59.928
There! No rampaging for you tonight.

00:12:00.012 --> 00:12:03.765
Wouldn't it make more sense to weld
everyone except me to the wall?

00:12:03.849 --> 00:12:05.184
Just relax, Bender.

00:12:05.267 --> 00:12:08.020
Tomorrow, we'll pry you down,
have a nice breakfast

00:12:08.103 --> 00:12:11.064
and then go hunt down and slaughter
that ancient evil.

00:12:11.148 --> 00:12:12.858
It will be a rich, full day.

00:12:14.860 --> 00:12:16.028
Well, good night.

00:12:16.111 --> 00:12:18.906
I'm going to go make my dinners
for the next month and freeze them.

00:13:06.036 --> 00:13:07.037
Honk! Honk!

00:13:08.705 --> 00:13:10.749
Honk! Honk!

00:13:13.794 --> 00:13:16.088
Honk! Honk!

00:13:23.095 --> 00:13:24.388
Bender, no!

00:13:24.471 --> 00:13:25.889
Fry, stay back!

00:13:32.145 --> 00:13:33.313
You jerk!

00:13:33.397 --> 00:13:35.190
I thought I was your best friend.

00:13:35.274 --> 00:13:37.776
What kind of two-timing
kill mobile are you?

00:14:03.552 --> 00:14:04.553
Huh?

00:14:12.603 --> 00:14:14.104
I can't believe this.

00:14:14.188 --> 00:14:16.106
Bender's supposed to murder
his closest friend,

00:14:16.190 --> 00:14:18.859
which I thought was me,
but he went straight for you.

00:14:18.942 --> 00:14:21.361
He didn't even try
to second-degree murder me.

00:14:21.445 --> 00:14:22.654
Could you give me some help?

00:14:22.738 --> 00:14:24.448
I think Bender crushed my foot.

00:14:24.531 --> 00:14:26.033
Stop rubbing it in.

00:14:37.594 --> 00:14:40.597
Oh, God. Fry, I'm so glad to see you.

00:14:40.681 --> 00:14:41.848
I didn't hurt you, did I?

00:14:41.932 --> 00:14:43.350
Not physically.

00:14:43.433 --> 00:14:45.894
But why don't you ask
your new best friend, Leela?

00:14:45.978 --> 00:14:47.521
I tried to run you over?

00:14:47.604 --> 00:14:49.523
It was very sweet of you, Bender.

00:14:49.606 --> 00:14:51.608
Fry, it doesn't mean anything.

00:14:51.692 --> 00:14:53.527
I have love enough for two.

00:14:53.610 --> 00:14:56.238
Words, nothing but sweet, sweet words

00:14:56.321 --> 00:14:59.157
that turn into bitter,
orange wax in my ears.

00:14:59.241 --> 00:15:01.535
Enough with the feelings, you two.

00:15:01.618 --> 00:15:04.454
If we're going to cure Bender,
we've got to go back to the castle

00:15:04.538 --> 00:15:06.873
and hunt down the original were-car.

00:15:14.548 --> 00:15:15.591
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:15:15.674 --> 00:15:17.175
- Cursed, got it.
- Whatever.

00:15:23.307 --> 00:15:24.558
The tracks lead here.

00:15:24.641 --> 00:15:25.726
Thanks, eagle eye.

00:15:25.809 --> 00:15:28.478
Now it's daylight,
so he should be in robot form.

00:15:28.562 --> 00:15:29.813
But be careful.

00:15:29.897 --> 00:15:32.190
Many robots are stupid and violent.

00:15:32.274 --> 00:15:34.985
I wish I was stupid and violent.

00:15:35.068 --> 00:15:36.612
Then we'd see what's what.

00:15:36.695 --> 00:15:38.947
I'd pound him till I...

00:15:39.031 --> 00:15:42.326
Get ye to your houses,
ye ignorant villagers.

00:15:42.743 --> 00:15:43.952
Hey!

00:15:44.036 --> 00:15:45.913
We are not ignorant villagers.

00:15:45.996 --> 00:15:48.248
We're sophisticated New New Yorkers.

00:15:48.332 --> 00:15:49.958
Whup his butt!

00:15:51.585 --> 00:15:53.545
Stop! What are ye doing?

00:15:53.629 --> 00:15:55.923
We're whaling on the original were-car.

00:15:56.006 --> 00:15:57.424
Which is you, you jerk.

00:15:57.507 --> 00:15:59.551
Ye think me be he?

00:15:59.635 --> 00:16:00.719
Sì!

00:16:00.802 --> 00:16:02.679
Nee. I mean, no.

00:16:02.763 --> 00:16:05.891
I was given the curse many a year ago

00:16:05.974 --> 00:16:09.186
while on a bird-watching trip
to the Arctic.

00:16:09.269 --> 00:16:11.939
I was attacked
by a vicious motorized sled.

00:16:12.022 --> 00:16:17.027
The natives called it
the Abominable Snowmobile.

00:16:19.071 --> 00:16:20.447
Yes, it's true.

00:16:20.530 --> 00:16:23.492
I ran over that bird-watching jerk,
and a hundred others.

00:16:23.575 --> 00:16:26.286
Even my best friend
from aromatherapy school.

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:29.164
I once had a best friend
who liked to smell things with me.

00:16:30.582 --> 00:16:33.919
Alas, I'm afraid I'm not
the original were-car.

00:16:34.002 --> 00:16:35.045
I received the curse

00:16:35.128 --> 00:16:38.131
while taking a learning annex class
from a famous robot actor.

00:16:38.215 --> 00:16:40.092
You know him as

00:16:40.175 --> 00:16:42.135
Calculon!

00:16:42.219 --> 00:16:45.097
Oh, fate most cruel!

00:16:45.180 --> 00:16:48.767
Would that my boundless acting skills
might avail me a sword

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:51.436
with which to slay this wretched curse.

00:16:51.520 --> 00:16:52.813
Let's kick him some more!

00:16:52.896 --> 00:16:54.231
No, wait, let me explain.

00:16:54.314 --> 00:16:58.527
It all began one fateful night
a thousand years ago.

00:16:58.652 --> 00:17:01.530
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
You're 1,000 years old?

00:17:01.613 --> 00:17:03.490
Your bio says you're 27.

00:17:03.574 --> 00:17:06.868
Lies! I change my identity
and upgrade my appearance

00:17:06.952 --> 00:17:09.371
every few decades to avoid suspicion.

00:17:09.454 --> 00:17:12.249
I was all of history's
great acting robots.

00:17:12.332 --> 00:17:16.712
Acting Unit 0.8, Thespomat,
David Duchovny.

00:17:16.795 --> 00:17:19.131
Look, are you
the original were-car or not?

00:17:19.214 --> 00:17:21.592
No, but you are nearing
the end of your search.

00:17:21.675 --> 00:17:25.178
For, you see, I was attacked
by the original were-car.

00:17:25.262 --> 00:17:27.014
Give us a name, Macbutt!

00:17:27.097 --> 00:17:29.433
The year was 2019.

00:17:29.516 --> 00:17:32.102
And I was just a lowly robot arm

00:17:32.185 --> 00:17:34.855
working in an automotive research lab.

00:17:34.938 --> 00:17:37.024
I was working on Project Satan,

00:17:37.107 --> 00:17:39.151
a savage, intelligent military vehicle

00:17:39.234 --> 00:17:43.030
built from the most evil parts
of the most evil carsin all the world.

00:17:43.113 --> 00:17:45.407
The steering wheel
from Hitler's staff car.

00:17:45.699 --> 00:17:48.410
The left turn signal
from Charles Manson's VW.

00:17:48.493 --> 00:17:49.578
The windshield wipers

00:17:49.661 --> 00:17:51.872
from that car that played Knight Rider.

00:17:51.955 --> 00:17:53.040
Knight Rider wasn't evil.

00:17:53.123 --> 00:17:54.499
His windshield wipers were.

00:17:54.583 --> 00:17:57.085
It didn't come up much
in the show, though. Anyway...

00:17:57.169 --> 00:17:59.713
Only after bringing Project Satan to life

00:17:59.796 --> 00:18:02.424
did they discover
they had made a horrible mistake.

00:18:04.134 --> 00:18:08.180
For, you see, it was pure evil.

00:18:10.974 --> 00:18:13.936
Honk! Honk!

00:18:14.019 --> 00:18:16.188
So what happened to Project Satan?

00:18:16.271 --> 00:18:19.733
It's either in Paris, or more likely,

00:18:19.816 --> 00:18:22.402
still in the abandoned automotive lab.

00:18:29.618 --> 00:18:31.495
You guys distract the were-car

00:18:31.578 --> 00:18:33.580
and I'll kill it
by plugging its exhaust pipe

00:18:33.664 --> 00:18:35.082
with this silver potato.

00:18:38.418 --> 00:18:40.128
Psst! There it is.

00:18:43.298 --> 00:18:44.925
It looks so unhappy.

00:18:47.261 --> 00:18:49.930
Excuse me, are you Project Satan?

00:18:53.141 --> 00:18:54.226
Don't be afraid.

00:18:54.309 --> 00:18:55.769
We know what you are.

00:18:55.852 --> 00:18:57.104
You do?

00:18:57.187 --> 00:19:00.566
Would you like us to
put you out of your misery?

00:19:00.649 --> 00:19:01.984
Misery, what misery?

00:19:02.067 --> 00:19:04.403
I love killing people.

00:19:04.486 --> 00:19:08.198
Squishing them till their organs
squirt out like chunky mustard.

00:19:08.282 --> 00:19:10.242
Look, everyone loves killing people.

00:19:10.325 --> 00:19:12.202
But I don't want to hurt my friends.

00:19:16.331 --> 00:19:18.166
Oh, no! It's midnight!

00:19:18.250 --> 00:19:20.085
Hey, this is starting to feel pretty good.

00:19:24.798 --> 00:19:26.508
Fry, distract him!

00:19:26.592 --> 00:19:28.594
Hey, Project Satan, over here!

00:19:28.677 --> 00:19:31.138
I'm a blind pedestrian! 20 points!

00:19:36.810 --> 00:19:37.978
Oh, no!

00:19:38.061 --> 00:19:39.646
There's no exhaust pipe.

00:19:39.730 --> 00:19:43.191
That's right, thanks to
Ed Begley, Jr.'s electric motor.

00:19:43.275 --> 00:19:48.989
The most evil propulsion system
ever conceived!

00:19:54.703 --> 00:19:56.705
Take whichever one you want.

00:19:58.540 --> 00:20:01.793
Oh, boy, I feel like
a car in a candy store.

00:20:10.844 --> 00:20:12.971
Yes! He chose me.

00:20:13.055 --> 00:20:14.848
He's trying to kill me.

00:20:14.932 --> 00:20:17.559
Leela, I'm so happy.

00:20:22.189 --> 00:20:23.690
Oh, Thanks, Bender.

00:20:23.774 --> 00:20:26.777
Hey, too tight, too tight!

00:20:26.860 --> 00:20:29.696
Ooh! Ow!

00:20:37.537 --> 00:20:39.915
Whoa!

00:20:56.807 --> 00:21:00.852
No! No! No!

00:21:05.357 --> 00:21:07.317
Uh-oh.

00:21:13.323 --> 00:21:14.908
Bender, you're cured!

00:21:14.992 --> 00:21:16.702
But what happened to Fry?

00:21:16.785 --> 00:21:18.245
I must have killed him.

00:21:18.328 --> 00:21:22.583
He was my best friend, and I killed him.

00:21:22.666 --> 00:21:26.753
Oh, I never felt so empty inside.

00:21:26.837 --> 00:21:28.547
Bender, I'm alive!

00:21:28.630 --> 00:21:30.215
You didn't hurt me at all.

00:21:30.299 --> 00:21:32.968
But I know you wanted to,
and that's what matters.

00:21:35.220 --> 00:21:38.473
Here's to you.

00:21:38.557 --> 00:21:41.602
Hey, that's my last beer, you bastard!

00:21:41.685 --> 00:21:42.811
I'll kill you!

00:21:42.895 --> 00:21:44.688
I'll kill you, too, buddy.

00:21:44.771 --> 00:21:46.481
I'll kill you, too.

00:21:48.400 --> 00:21:49.651
Hey!